itive mothers and their children in sub-Saharan Africa.</article-title><source>Bull WHO</source><volume>84</volume><fpage>546</fpage><lpage>554</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16878228</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002454-Thior1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thior</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Lockman</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Smeaton</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Shapiro</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Wester</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Breastfeeding plus infant zidovudine prophylaxis for 6 months vs formula feeding plus infant zidovudine for 1 month to reduce mother-to-child transmission in Botswana.</article-title><source>JAMA</source><volume>296</volume><fpage>794</fpage><lpage>805</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16905785</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002454-Coutinho1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Coutinho</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Cabral de Lira</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>de Carvalho Lima</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ashworth</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Comparison of the effect of two systems for the promotion of exclusive breastfeeding.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>366</volume><fpage>1094</fpage><lpage>1100</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16182897</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002454-Haider1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haider</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ashworth</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kabir</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Huttly</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Effect of community-based peer counsellors on exclusive breastfeeding practices in Dhaka, Bangladesh: a randomised controlled trial.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>356</volume><fpage>1643</fpage><lpage>1647</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11089824</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002454-Morrow1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Morrow</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Guerrero</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Shults</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Calva</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Lutter</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Efficacy of home-based peer counselling to promote exclusive breastfeeding: a randomised controlled trial.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>353</volume><fpage>1226</fpage><lpage>1231</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10217083</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002454-Bland1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bland</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Becquet</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Rollins</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Coutsoudis</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Coovadia</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Breast health problems are rare in both HIV-infected and HIV-uninfected women who receive counseling and support for breast-feeding in South Africa.</article-title><source>CID</source><volume>45</volume><fpage>1502</fpage><lpage>1510</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002454-Bland2"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bland</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Little</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Coovadia</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Coutsoudis</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rollins</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Intervention to promote exclusive breastfeeding for the first 6 months of life in a high HIV prevalence area.</article-title><publisher-name>AIDS In Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002454-Bland3"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bland</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Rollins</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Coovadia</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Coutsoudis</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Newell</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Infant feeding counselling for HIV-infected and uninfected women: appropriateness of choice and practice.</article-title><source>Bull WHO</source><volume>85</volume><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>296</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17546310</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002454-Rice1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rice</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Batzing-Feigenbaum</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hosegood</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanser</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Hill</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Population and antenatal-based HIV prevalence estimates in a high contracepting female population in South Africa.</article-title><source>BMC Public Health</source><volume>7(1)</volume><fpage>160</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17640354</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002454-UNAIDSWHO1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>UNAIDS/WHO</collab><year>2005</year><article-title>AIDS Epidemic Update. www/unaids.org/epi/2005/doc/report_pdf.: UNAIDS, Geneva.</article-title></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002454-WHOUNICEF1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>WHO/UNICEF</collab><year>1993</year><article-title>Breastfeeding counselling: A training course. Trainer's Guide: World Health Organization, Geneva.</article-title></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002454-WHOUNICEFUNAIDS1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>WHO/UNICEF/UNAIDS</collab><year>2000</year><article-title>HIV and infant feeding counselling: a training course. Trainers' Guide.</article-title></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002454-Skordis1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Skordis</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Nattrass</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Paying to waste lives: the affordability of reducing mother-to-child transmission of HIV in South Africa.</article-title><source>Journal of Health Economics</source><volume>21</volume><fpage>405</fpage><lpage>421</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12022266</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002454-Sweat1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sweat</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Reilly</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmid</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Denison</surname><given-names>J</giv